<title>CANADA: Canada April department store sales fall on month.</title>
<headline>Canada April department store sales fall on month.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian department stores sales fell a seasonally adjusted 0.01 percent in April from March to C$1.29 billion, Statistics Canada said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In unadjusted data, year-over-year sales in rose 9.2 percent to C$1.15 billion.</p>
<p>The agency said that it would no longer provide sales figures broken down into major and discount department stores.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Statistics Canada, Louise Genereux, Retail Trade Section, 613-951-3549.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
